# Node.js & Express.js Rules

## Express Application Bootstrap
- Create the Express `app` in `src/app.js`; start the server in `src/server.js`.
- Never call `app.listen()` inside `app.js` — keep them separate for testability.

```js
// src/app.js
import express from 'express';
import helmet from 'helmet';
import compression from 'compression';
import { errorHandler } from './middlewares/error-handler.js';
import { requestLogger } from './middlewares/request-logger.js';
import userRoutes from './routes/user-routes.js';

const app = express();
app.use(helmet());
app.use(compression());
app.use(express.json({ limit: '1mb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));
app.use(requestLogger);

app.use('/api/v1/users', userRoutes);

app.use(errorHandler); // must be last
export default app;
```

## Routing Rules
- All routes live in `src/routes/`.
- Route files only wire HTTP verbs → controller methods; zero business logic.
- Validate request schema at the route level using `zod` or `joi` before hitting the controller.
- Version all routes: `/api/v1/`, `/api/v2/`.

```js
// src/routes/user-routes.js
import { Router } from 'express';
import { validate } from '../middlewares/validate.js';
import { createUserSchema } from '../validators/user-validator.js';
import { UserController } from '../controllers/user-controller.js';

const router = Router();
const ctrl = new UserController();

router.get('/:id', ctrl.getById);
router.post('/', validate(createUserSchema), ctrl.create);
router.put('/:id', validate(updateUserSchema), ctrl.update);
router.delete('/:id', ctrl.remove);

export default router;
```

## Controller Rules
- Controllers must be **thin**: parse input, call service, return response.
- Always wrap service calls with `try/catch` and forward errors to `next(err)`.
- Return consistent JSON envelopes.

```js
// src/controllers/user-controller.js
export class UserController {
  constructor(userService) {
    this.userService = userService;
    // bind methods for Express compatibility
    this.getById = this.getById.bind(this);
    this.create  = this.create.bind(this);
  }

  async getById(req, res, next) {
    try {
      const user = await this.userService.findById(req.params.id);
      res.json({ success: true, data: user });
    } catch (err) {
      next(err);
    }
  }

  async create(req, res, next) {
    try {
      const user = await this.userService.create(req.body);
      res.status(201).json({ success: true, data: user });
    } catch (err) {
      next(err);
    }
  }
}
```

## Middleware Rules
- Every middleware must call `next()` or send a response — never both.
- Async middleware must catch errors and pass to `next(err)`.
- Order: security (helmet) → CORS → body-parser → auth → rate-limit → routes → error-handler.

## Error Handling
- Use a custom error hierarchy in `src/errors/`.
- The global error handler middleware must be the last `app.use()`.

```js
// src/errors/app-error.js
export class AppError extends Error {
  constructor(message, statusCode, code) {
    super(message);
    this.statusCode = statusCode;
    this.code = code;
    this.isOperational = true;
    Error.captureStackTrace(this, this.constructor);
  }
}
export class NotFoundError extends AppError {
  constructor(resource) {
    super(`${resource} not found`, 404, 'NOT_FOUND');
  }
}
export class ValidationError extends AppError {
  constructor(message) {
    super(message, 422, 'VALIDATION_ERROR');
  }
}

// src/middlewares/error-handler.js
export function errorHandler(err, req, res, next) {
  const statusCode = err.statusCode ?? 500;
  const code       = err.code ?? 'INTERNAL_ERROR';
  if (!err.isOperational) console.error('[Unhandled]', err);
  res.status(statusCode).json({ success: false, error: { code, message: err.message } });
}
```

## Security Essentials
- Always use `helmet()`.
- Rate-limit all public endpoints with `express-rate-limit`.
- Sanitize user input — never interpolate raw strings into queries.
- Set `CORS` explicitly; never use `origin: '*'` in production.
- Validate `Content-Type` on POST/PUT routes.

## Performance
- Enable `compression` middleware.
- Use `keep-alive` connections for DB pools.
- Avoid synchronous operations (`fs.readFileSync`, `JSON.parse` on large payloads) in request path.
- Stream large responses with `res.pipe()`.

## Environment Config

```js
// src/config/env.js
import { z } from 'zod';
import dotenv from 'dotenv';
dotenv.config();

const envSchema = z.object({
  NODE_ENV:   z.enum(['development', 'test', 'production']),
  PORT:       z.coerce.number().default(3000),
  DB_HOST:    z.string(),
  DB_PORT:    z.coerce.number().default(3306),
  DB_NAME:    z.string(),
  DB_USER:    z.string(),
  DB_PASS:    z.string(),
  MONGO_URI:  z.string().url(),
  ASB_CONN:   z.string(), // Azure Service Bus connection string
});

export const env = envSchema.parse(process.env);
```
